  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Creating Golden-winged Warbler Habitat in MN PP</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is part of a long-term, multi-partner initiative to reduce threats to the Golden-winged Warbler through conservation actions taken throughout its range. It will restore 1,192 acres of high quality young forest breeding habitat in a Golden-winged Warbler focal area in Minnesota. The project will also train public and private foresters operating in Golden-winged Warbler focal areas in new best management practices and how to implement them. The long-term goal of the project is to meet Golden-winged Warbler population goals by 2050 by creating an estimated 9,000 new acres of breeding habitat annually in Minnesota.</narrative>
  </description>
